// Two blooms three apart grew into one slab; its width gives both stones. Acid, a fenced ember and spikes on the way; spouts and acid past it.
name Fused Bloom
rule B1234/S012345678
steps 2
hint Two seeds lie on the road, on the ledges. The outline in the trench is one slab, but no single bloom is that wide. Two stones, close together, grew into each other.
tip A bloom is five wide. An eight-wide slab is two blooms three apart: the stones are two in from the left edge and two in from the right. Plant both, get clear, grow.
intro Two beginnings so close that their blooms fused. The road here has learned to bite: green pools, spikes, an ember with a short leash.
outro Two seeds, one slab. Nothing that grows keeps to itself.
say wake|The pool ahead is not water. Jump it.
say seed|A seed. There will be two; this shape needed two.
say plant|One seed in. The other goes three cells from it, or the slab comes out wrong.
say grow|Both at once. If it is red at either end, one of them is off by one.
say found|Fused. Two blooms, one ground. Up you go.
say die|Again. Slower, this time.
